{"base_rate":0.36351706036745407,"brier":0.14977007874015746,"bss":0.3526882459339761,"bss_hi":0.446944656650162,"bss_lo":0.2600268036769446,"chart":{"base":[533.4,57.9],"fp":[293.0,313.8],"lead":"62,256.4 272,229.5 482,177.2 692,115.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.35 — higher than 66% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +13pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 57% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 8%; promised 97% → rained 83%"},"rel":"62,429.5 142.4,370.9 462.4,217.9 672.3,107.4"},"country":"FR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09291338582677167,"ess":369.2064045708967,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Toulouse</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Toulouse rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTOULOUSE-BLAGNAC, 5.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.35, ranked 73 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(38&ndash;124) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>296</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>159</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Toulouse</b> <span class=\"muted\">France</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.35</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>38&ndash;124\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Toulouse &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Toulouse\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 73.1335,350.15 133.63949367088605,271.4177215189873 236.70103896103896,155.0909090909091 333.172676056338,64.14084507042253 400.9569811320755,20.289308176100633 400.9569811320755,38.66100628930815 333.172676056338,135.9154929577465 236.70103896103896,240.1818181818182 133.63949367088605,335.9240506329114 73.1335,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"249.6797900262467\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"249.6797900262467\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,351.2567567567568 73.1335,331.95 133.63949367088605,271.4177215189873 236.70103896103896,202.36363636363637 333.172676056338,141.04225352112675 400.9569811320755,79.81132075471697\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 296 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"351.2567567567568\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"73.1335\" cy=\"331.95\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 21%&amp;#10;It rained 30% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"133.63949367088605\" cy=\"271.4177215189873\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"236.70103896103896\" cy=\"202.36363636363637\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.172676056338\" cy=\"141.04225352112675\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 159 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"400.9569811320755\" cy=\"79.81132075471697\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(36%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Toulouse the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.153</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.271</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.313</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.585</td><td class='num'>3.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.60426,"lon":1.44367,"n":762,"n_cities":213,"name":"Toulouse","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":296,"obs":0.08445945945945946,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.04275,"n":80,"obs":0.1375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.38,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.2136708860759493,"n":79,"obs":0.3037974683544304,"sig":false},{"hi":0.68,"lo":0.38,"mean":0.5048051948051948,"n":77,"obs":0.49350649350